                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "63a18aa4-3055-320b-90a5-56104a2ec6bc",
                        "entry_id": "88a22b06-0d01-3d53-8daa-a4249684c0ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A type of dumpling served in Turkish, Armenian and Central Asian cuisine"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "071f70a0-d484-4544-b80c-76c92a1aeef8",
                                "sense_id": "63a18aa4-3055-320b-90a5-56104a2ec6bc",
                                "text": "And they kept one of the national dishes, manti (pasta stuffed with ground beef served in garlic-yogurt sauce, $11.50), as well as lahmacun, sort of a Turkish pizza ($3), and arnavut cigeri (fried calf's liver and potatoes, $5.75), a hot appetizer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bfdf21d0-a372-4f70-8b57-e2dfeeeb80c0",
                                "sense_id": "63a18aa4-3055-320b-90a5-56104a2ec6bc",
                                "text": "Crowding the table were miniature, hand-formed lamb dumplings called manti; flaky pastries, called boreks, filled with wild greens; and an elaborate paste of chicken, wheat and pistachios called keskek."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
